{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And one who strikes his father and his mother.</b> Since Scripture taught us regarding one who wounds his fellow that he is liable to compensation and not to death, it was necessary to state regarding one who wounds his father that he is liable to death — and he is liable only for a blow that produces a wound." "<b>His father and his mother.</b> Either this one or that one." "<b>He shall surely be put to death.</b> By strangling (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:33.729694801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}